I have looked at the data sheets for the SCT3258 before and it does look like an interesting chip. CML Microcircuits is a UK company so there might be some support available, and maybe even some example applications, but often that comes along with non-disclosure agreements which might make an open source project difficult. <br><br>None of the current developers has the time (or inclination) to take this on but it certainly looks as if it might be possible given enough effort. <br><br>You have also found one of the other problems with the Chinese radios. The manufacturers often change the design completely and still keep the original model number.  <br><br>Colin G4EML<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=87">G4EML</a> — Wed Nov 22, 2023 5:59 pm</p><hr />
